        <mxCell id="6jMXHIdN_H4GYaneC3hk-29" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;FigR. Functional ingerence of gene regulation. 1) pair scATAC-se with scRNA-seq; 2) connect cis-reg elements to target genes; 3) identify TF-gene relationships&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;*Generate ~91k blood cells scRAN and scATAC&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;*First map cells from scRNA to scATAC using in-paper developed tool named &quot;scOptMatch&quot;. Using these data, they found chromatian accessiblity at distal peaks is highly cell type specific, even more so than gene expression.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;GWAS → DORC → TF → 已知 SLE 基因. DORC: domain of regulatory chromatain&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;2075&quot; data-end=&quot;2102&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;2077&quot; data-end=&quot;2102&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;2077&quot; data-end=&quot;2102&quot;&gt;DORCs = GWAS 风险的调控承载体&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;2103&quot; data-end=&quot;2123&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;2105&quot; data-end=&quot;2123&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;2105&quot; data-end=&quot;2123&quot;&gt;TFs = 风险变异的执行者&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;li data-start=&quot;2124&quot; data-end=&quot;2156&quot;&gt;&lt;p data-start=&quot;2126&quot; data-end=&quot;2156&quot;&gt;&lt;strong data-start=&quot;2126&quot; data-end=&quot;2156&quot;&gt;GRN = 把遗传风险翻译成细胞状态和调控机制的中介&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/li&gt;&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; color: rgb(31, 31, 31); font-family: ElsevierGulliver, Georgia, &amp;quot;Times New Roman&amp;quot;, Times, STIXGeneral, &amp;quot;Cambria Math&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Lucida Sans Unicode&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Microsoft Sans Serif&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Segoe UI Symbol&amp;quot;, &amp;quot;Arial Unicode MS&amp;quot;, serif, sans-serif; font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;Prior epigenomic studies have extensively utilized&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/biochemistry-genetics-and-molecular-biology/volume&quot; title=&quot;Learn more about bulk from ScienceDirect&#39;s AI-generated Topic Pages&quot; class=&quot;topic-link&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); word-break: break-word; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-decoration-color: rgb(31, 31, 31); color: rgb(31, 31, 31); text-underline-offset: 1px;&quot;&gt;bulk&lt;/a&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px;&quot;&gt;&amp;nbsp;analysis of&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.sciencedirect.com/topics/biochemistry-genetics-and-molecular-biology/histone-modification&quot; title=&quot;Learn more about histone modifications from ScienceDirect&#39;s AI-generated Topic Pages&quot; class=&quot;topic-link&quot; style=&quot;box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0px; padding: 0px; background-color: rgba(0, 0, 0, 0); word-break: break-word; text-decoration-thickness: 1px; text-decoration-color: rgb(31, 31, 31); color: rgb(31, 31, 31); text-underline-offset: 1px;&quot;&gt;histone modifications&lt;/a&gt;, chromatin accessibility, and genome topology to annotate the function of disease-associated non-coding genetic variation.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;a class=&quot;anchor anchor-primary&quot; href=&quot;https://www.s