        <mxCell id="XOWEwEKvRYx0S_CinpEg-1" parent="1" style="text;html=1;whiteSpace=wrap;strokeColor=none;fillColor=none;align=left;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=0;" value="&lt;h3 class=&quot;c-article-box__container-title u-h3 js-expandable-title&quot; id=&quot;Sec5&quot; style=&quot;-webkit-font-smoothing: antialiased; font-family: Harding, Palatino, serif; letter-spacing: -0.0117156rem; line-height: 1.4rem; box-sizing: inherit; margin-bottom: 8px; color: rgb(34, 34, 34); background-color: rgb(255, 255, 255);&quot;&gt;&lt;font style=&quot;font-size: 16px;&quot;&gt;Box 1 Binding motif databases and motif matcher algorithms&lt;/font&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Inferences&lt;/b&gt;: bulk Expr;&amp;nbsp; TF binding and bulk chromatin accessibility; Single-cell transcriptomics data&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Downstream GRN analyses:&amp;nbsp;&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*Topological analysis (&lt;b&gt;network centrality&lt;/b&gt;, TF drive cell fate changes in diverse biological contexts; &lt;b&gt;spectral graph theory, GRN as a matrix, non-negative matrix factorization to find groups of TFs with certain functionality&lt;/b&gt;)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*Comparative analysis (to identify &lt;b&gt;rewiring events different from cell types, states, etc.&lt;/b&gt;&amp;nbsp;)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*Inference of TF activities (+ gene expression into TF topology to infer which TF to have relevant role in certain contexts. Enrichment)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*Perturbation and prediction of cell fate ()&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Experimental assessment of GRNs&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*TF abundance and post-translational modification (Transcripts are a proxy of protein abundance, let alone activity; single-cell proteomics is still challenging, but spatial proteomics is possible but costly.)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*TF binding and cooperativity&amp;nbsp; (&lt;b&gt;TF assigned to the chromatin regions&lt;/b&gt; based on its binding motif. However, TF motif may have low specificity, so &lt;b&gt;ChIP-seq&lt;/b&gt; data are necessary as it provide more accurate binding info than motif.)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*Regulatory activity of CREs (MPRA)&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*Linkage to target genes&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;*TF perturbation&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;&lt;b&gt;Challenges and future directions&lt;/b&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Integrating transcription and accessibility&amp;nbsp;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Scale and sparsity of single-cell data&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;The regulatory of 3D genome structure&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Refinement of TF binding predictions&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Emerging multi-omics for GRN inference&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;Benchmarking of GRNs&lt;/div&gt;&lt;div&gt;GRNs in the bigger picture (intracell and intercell with spartial infor)&lt;/div&gt;" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="155" width="534" x="1396" y="545" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
        <mxCell id="XOWEwEKvRYx0S_CinpEg-2" parent="1" style="triangle;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;" value="" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="56" width="40" x="1346" y="594" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
      </root>
    </mxGraphModel>
